<!-- wp:kadence/advancedheading {"uniqueID":"9_693b72-e4","htmlTag":"p","className":"bp-lead t-p"} -->
<p class="kt-adv-heading9_693b72-e4 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading bp-lead t-p" data-kb-block="kb-adv-heading9_693b72-e4">A shopper finds the product they want, picks a size, and sees <b>"Out of stock"</b>. <span class="ac">What happens next decides whether you ever see that sale.</span></p>
<!-- /wp:kadence/advancedheading -->

<!-- wp:kadence/advancedheading {"uniqueID":"9_f216b2-21","htmlTag":"p","className":"t-p"} -->
<p class="kt-adv-heading9_f216b2-21 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading t-p" data-kb-block="kb-adv-heading9_f216b2-21">Most stores give that shopper nothing to do. There is no button, no date, no way to stay in touch. So they leave, search for the same product somewhere else, and buy it there.</p>
<!-- /wp:kadence/advancedheading -->

<!-- wp:kadence/advancedheading {"uniqueID":"9_3a5759-0b","htmlTag":"p","className":"t-p"} -->
<p class="kt-adv-heading9_3a5759-0b wp-block-kadence-advancedheading t-p" data-kb-block="kb-adv-heading9_3a5759-0b">A stockout is not the end of the sale. It is a pause. Back in stock alerts turn that pause into a list of people who have already said "I want this", and bring them back the moment you restock.</p>
<!-- /wp:kadence/advancedheading -->

<!-- wp:kadence/column {"uniqueID":"9_f5b891-70","direction":["vertical","",""],"rowGap":[0,"",""],"rowGapVariable":["custom","",""],"kbVersion":2,"className":"bp-compare rv t-div"} -->
